From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:43:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: Add the RK3528 VDPP scaler

The RK3528's VDPP is a video post-processor with a polyphase scaler,
which mainline has no driver for. Add a mem2mem driver scaling an NV12
frame to the CAPTURE size with the filters Rockchip's MPP gives the
vendor kernel, its enhancement off.

The VDPP is one engine with the IEP2: the same clocks, resets, interrupt
and IOMMU. The driver takes the shared resets released and acquires them
while streaming, so a second user of the engine gets -EBUSY at STREAMON,
and answers the interrupt only while in use and in its own work mode.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
